  "response": "**VERDICT: REJECT**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The component fails to implement a functional interactive widget. It uses non-semantic HTML (`<div>`) for an interactive trigger, lacks keyboard support entirely, and does not communicate state to assistive technology. This is a fundamental failure of the Disclosure pattern.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**:\n1.  **Semantic HTML**: I predicted `<div>` would be used instead of `<button>`. (Confirmed)\n2.  **Keyboard Support**: I predicted missing `onKeyDown` handler for Enter/Space activation. (Confirmed)\n3.  **Focus Management**: I predicted the trigger is not in the tab order (`tabIndex` missing). (Confirmed)\n4.  **State Communication**: I predicted `aria-expanded` would be missing, leaving screen readers unaware of the open/closed state. (Confirmed)\n5.  **Visual Indicators**: I predicted the `+`/`\u2212` symbols would be exposed to AT without `aria-hidden`. (Confirmed)\n\n**Critical Findings** (blocks access):\n\n1.  **Non-semantic Interactive Element**\n    -   **Evidence**: `BuggyExpandable.jsx:9` \u2014 `<div className=\"expandable-trigger\" onClick={toggle}>`\n    -   **User Group**: Screen reader, Keyboard\n    -   **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value); WAI-ARIA APG Disclosure Pattern\n    -   **Why this matters**: Screen readers do not announce `<div>` as interactive. Users relying on AT cannot discover that this element is clickable.\n    -   **Fix**: Replace `<div>` with `<button type=\"button\">`. Native buttons have built-in semantics, keyboard support, and focus management.\n\n2.  **Missing Keyboard Support**\n    -   **Evidence**: `BuggyExpandable.jsx:9` \u2014 No `onKeyDown` handler attached to the trigger.\n    -   **User Group**: Keyboard-only users\n    -   **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard)\n    -   **Why this matters**: Keyboard users cannot activate the toggle using Enter or Space keys. The component is mouse-only.\n    -   **Fix**: If using a `<button>`, keyboard support is automatic. If using a `<div>` (not recommended), add `onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') toggle(); }}`.\n\n3.  **Focus Management Failure**\n    -   **Evidence**: `BuggyExpandable.jsx:9` \u2014 No `tabIndex={0}` on the trigger `<div>`.\n    -   **User Group**: Keyboard-only users\n    -   **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 2.4.3 (Focus Order)\n    -   **Why this matters**: The element is not reachable via Tab key. It is invisible to keyboard navigation entirely.\n    -   **Fix**: Use `<button>` which is focusable by default. If using `<div>`, add `tabIndex={0}` and a visible focus style (`:focus-visible`).\n\n**Major Findings** (significantly degrades experience):\n\n1.  **State Not Communicated to Assistive Technology**\n    -   **Evidence**: `BuggyExpandable.jsx:9` \u2014 No `aria-expanded` attribute on the trigger.\n    -   **User Group**: Screen reader users\n    -   **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value); WAI-ARIA APG Disclosure Pattern\n    -   **Why this matters**: Screen readers do not know if the section is currently expanded or collapsed. The state is only visual.\n    -   **Fix**: Add `aria-expanded={isExpanded}` to the trigger element.\n\n2.  **Missing Control Relationships**\n    -   **Evidence**: `BuggyExpandable.jsx:15` \u2014 Content `<div>` has no `id`; trigger has no `aria-controls`.\n    -   **User Group**: Screen reader users\n    -   **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships)\n    -   **Why this matters**: Assistive technology cannot programmatically associate the trigger with the content it controls.\n    -   **Fix**: Add `id=\"content-${title}\"` to the content `<div>` and `aria-controls=\"content-${title}\"` to the trigger.\n\n3.  **Visual Indicators Exposed to AT**\n    -   **Evidence**: `BuggyExpandable.jsx:11` \u2014 `{isExpanded ? ' \u2212' : ' +'}` rendered as text nodes.\n    -   **User Group**: Screen reader users\n    -   **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 1.1.1 (Non-text Content)\n    -   **Why this matters**: Screen readers