o specific zoom issue detected in code. Focus indicator missing makes tracking position difficult.\n-   **Cognitive accessibility**: The interaction model is ambiguous. Is it a link? A button? A header? Visual styling suggests clickability, but lack of standard affordances (underline, pointer cursor) creates uncertainty.\n\n**Verdict Justification**:\nThe component fails to meet the minimum requirements for an interactive widget. It lacks semantic HTML (`<button>`), keyboard operability, and state communication (`aria-expanded`). These are not minor gaps; they completely block access for keyboard and screen reader users. The design must be revised to use native semantics or implement a complete ARIA pattern.\n\n**Open Questions (unscored)**:\n-   Is the `title` prop unique enough to generate a stable `id` for `aria-controls`? If not, consider using a generated ID or React ref to avoid duplicate IDs in the DOM.",
